{"lines":[{"x":0.84101745676095518,"h":0.016225354269901682,"y":0.062839613766048852,"t":"Reading","c":1,"w":0.081515712738037149},{"h":0.016048292108362783,"c":1,"x":0.084362148237552032,"t":"One way to answer the question is to look at the music and not the neurons. While","w":0.77777776082356764,"y":0.10895170803206433},{"c":1,"x":0.084251333775675147,"y":0.12325406632820668,"t":"music can often seem (at least to the outsider) like a labyrinth of intricate patterns, it","w":0.79447723388671876,"h":0.022246296751204375},{"h":0.019689310565854212,"t":"turns out that the most important part of every song or symphony is when the patterns","w":0.81294250488281261,"y":0.14306381222741638,"c":1,"x":0.082209732193004939},{"t":"break down, when the sound becomes unpredictable. If the music is too obvious, it is","x":0.084362144522710125,"y":0.1627906975154092,"w":0.80246912638346357,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1},{"w":0.81687240600585931,"h":0.017462404653237007,"y":0.18021201410496968,"x":0.082304537609773451,"c":1,"t":"annoyingly boring, like an alarm clock. Numerous studies, after all, have demonstrated"},{"x":0.08230451405062221,"t":"that dopamine neurons quickly adapt to predictable rewards. If we know what's going","y":0.19758539480087878,"w":0.80452677408854167,"h":0.017667844522968323,"c":1},{"x":0.080246926243610239,"c":1,"w":0.78600819905598951,"y":0.21511627925665155,"t":"to happen next, then we don't get excited. This is why composers often introduce a","h":0.01751034054795475},{"y":0.23233379436562474,"w":0.81701243082682296,"c":1,"x":0.082225425680239064,"h":0.020270717158053619,"t":"key note in the beginning of a song, spend most of the rest of the piece in the studious"},{"c":1,"t":"avoidance of the pattern, and then finally repeat it only at the end. The longer we are","w":0.79850006103515614,"x":0.082235409649713057,"h":0.019450813356361341,"y":0.24971947192592803},{"y":0.26884570088458493,"h":0.017491508569256853,"t":"denied the pattern we expect, the greater the emotional release when the pattern","x":0.082304536922597524,"w":0.76543207804361979,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.23662551879882809,"y":0.28769140137985327,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.080246911285709974,"t":"returns, safe and sound."},{"h":0.018541769088367577,"w":0.78200815836588533,"c":1,"t":"To demonstrate this psychological principle, the musicologist Leonard Meyer, in his","x":0.082239376269987854,"y":0.31393384624375131},{"x":0.08017097993719205,"y":0.33099794302711283,"c":1,"h":0.020158828357925707,"w":0.78409978230794286,"t":"classic book Emotion and Meaning in Music (1956), analysed the 5th movement of"},{"x":0.082187201113491801,"y":0.34843603590946826,"h":0.020628770754109849,"c":1,"w":0.77799484252929685,"t":"Beethoven's String Quartet in C-sharp minor, Op. 131. Meyer wanted to show how"},{"c":1,"t":"music is defined by its flirtation with - but not submission to - our expectations of order.","x":0.080196056123991652,"y":0.36699889947275843,"h":0.018198737828554634,"w":0.82728510538736977},{"t":"Meyer dissected 50 measures (bars) of the masterpiece, showing how Beethoven","y":0.38408134117549042,"h":0.020703096693059142,"x":0.080153884886710033,"c":1,"w":0.77384231567382811},{"w":0.77995112101236996,"y":0.40252546272827172,"h":0.019115901807733371,"t":"begins with the clear statement of a rhythmic and harmonic pattern and then, in an","c":1,"x":0.080185914824721649},{"y":0.42137809200118204,"t":"ingenious tonal dance, carefully holds off repeating it. What Beethoven does instead is","x":0.078189294028255085,"w":0.81893005371093741,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"w":0.82098765055338541,"y":0.43895348820645586,"c":1,"x":0.080246915177451875,"t":"suggest variations of the pattern. He wants to preserve an element of uncertainty in his","h":0.017465828445129006},{"t":"music, making our brains beg for the one chord he refuses to give us. Beethoven saves","y":0.45639534867343801,"w":0.82716049194335928,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1,"x":0.080246914220143045},{"x":0.078189305486008609,"h":0.016014052504504717,"c":1,"t":"that chord for the end.","w":0.21604937235514321,"y":0.4752650173986197},{"w":0.81275721232096354,"x":0.078189294951564528,"t":"According to Meyer, it is the suspenseful tension of music, arising out of our unfulfilled","y":0.50290697658480499,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.80041147867838536,"t":"expectations, that is the source of the music's feeling. While earlier theories of music","h":0.018944996405827252,"x":0.080246935892288693,"y":0.51884570064055369},{"w":0.82510289510091139,"x":0.076131679774275374,"y":0.53769140136945315,"c":1,"t":"focused on the way a sound can refer to the real world of images and experiences - its","h":0.017667844522968212},{"y":0.55312476651767017,"t":"'connotative' meaning - Meyer argued that the emotions we find in music come from the","x":0.07594517890572007,"w":0.8357209777832032,"h":0.022863990145661983,"c":1},{"t":"unfolding events of the music itself. This 'embodied meaning' arises from the patterns","w":0.80876831054687504,"c":1,"x":0.078131891519990782,"y":0.56993206032034915,"h":0.021811349372279687},{"h":0.017441860778592888,"x":0.078189298695436379,"t":"the symphony invokes and then ignores. It is this uncertainty that triggers the surge","y":0.59156976727657218,"w":0.78806584676106772,"c":1},{"y":0.60896772584223113,"w":0.78199844360351567,"h":0.018503974267534917,"x":0.078134699343638842,"c":1,"t":"of dopamine in the caudate, as we struggle to figure out what will happen next. We"},{"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"y":0.62779740850443544,"w":0.81275721232096354,"t":"can predict some of the notes, but we can't predict them all, and that is what keeps us","x":0.078189294970564441},{"x":0.076131686804235515,"h":0.017489796673310742,"c":1,"t":"listening, waiting expectantly for our reward, for the pattern to be completed.","y":0.64534883704954649,"w":0.72427983601888013},{"t":"67","w":0.026748971939086874,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.88683127525302174,"y":0.93749999982794041,"c":1},{"x":0.394621061735003,"w":0.2086137517293295,"t":"leltsresources.org","c":1,"y":0.96588917689070863,"h":0.018370868741272584}],"h":3395,"w":2400}